post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
The systemd user unit is installed but deliberately not enabled:

  systemctl --user enable --now pw-live-danmaku

It publishes a PipeWire video node named "pw-live-danmaku" (480x1080, 30 fps) and
draws the chat of room 1746707149, which is upstream's own room -- change it, or
the overlay shows someone else's stream:

  systemctl --user edit pw-live-danmaku          # override ExecStart=

The room is a room number or a URL (https://live.bilibili.com/545068). Add
--cookie-file for real nicknames; Bilibili masks them on an anonymous connection.
Write that path with systemd's %h, never ~:

  --cookie-file %h/.config/pw-live-danmaku/cookie

Select the node from OBS with the obs-pwvideo plugin; the linux-pipewire plugin
shipped with OBS goes through xdg-desktop-portal and cannot see this kind of node.
Set the source size to exactly --size (480x1080): a smaller negotiated size is
clipped, not scaled.

The room starts empty, because a panel is a window rather than a log. --history N
keeps the last N rows on disk so the next start has something to show.

Options are the ExecStart arguments of the unit, e.g.

  pw-live-danmaku --help                        # full list
  pw-live-danmaku --demo --dump /tmp/panel.png  # render without a live room
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}